+## Styling: Tailwind, compiled per render
+
+Every style is a Tailwind v4 utility class. There is no inline style and no
+stylesheet in this package. A tree's classes are built at render time
+(`p-md`, `w-[182px]`, `md:flex-row`), so no build-time scan could find them.
+The CSS is compiled from the classes a render actually used, against the
+tenant's theme:
+
+```ts
+const { css: themeCss } = emitCss(theme, { surfaces }); // @fanos/tokens: vars, @theme, type-*, surface-*
+const markup = renderToStaticMarkup(<Render tree={tree} data={data} width={534} />);
+const css = await cssForMarkup(markup, themeCss);       // or cssForElement(<Render …/>, themeCss) in a Server Component
+```
+
+- **Tokens are theme keys.** `space.4` → `p-4`, `color.core_sec_500` →
+  `text-core-sec-500`. A tenant rethemes by changing the theme, never the
+  tree. Raw values become arbitrary values (`w-[28px]`) and set
+  `data-fos-raw`. Negative tokens use the negative utility (`-top-6`).
+  Percentages pass through and are not raw debt.
+- **`Resp<>` becomes one class per breakpoint**: `flex-col md:flex-row`.
+- **Composites yield.** `type-*` and `surface-*` (emitted by `@fanos/tokens`)
+  have zero specificity (`:where(.surface-x)`). The single-purpose utilities a
+  node or a component sets beside them always win, so a Divider's `border-0`
+  beats its surface's `border`.
+- **Client state is an attribute, never a class change.** Interactive
+  primitives use `data-[state=open]:…` and `aria-disabled:…` variants. Every
+  class an element can carry is in the server markup, so the compiled sheet
+  already has it. A client component receives its classes as props
+  (`className`, `*ClassName`, `classNames`), and `cssForElement` collects them
+  there.
+- No Tailwind default theme and no preflight: only the tenant's tokens exist.
+
